1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:04,921
Acetic acid ionises a little into acetate and hydrogen ions.

2
00:00:04,921 --> 00:00:10,299
Now add sodium acetate, a salt that floods the solution with acetate.

3
00:00:10,299 --> 00:00:12,500
The equilibrium shifts left.

4
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:19,882
Hydrogen ion concentration falls, and the p H rises, even though we added more acetic material.

